11
00:46:53,684 --> 00:46:59,684
The film's plot centers on a meteor that lands on Earth, which unleashes a
carnivorous alien that finds refuge in the basement of a house.

12
00:51:09,473 --> 00:51:15,473
As it grows larger, a young monster movie fan named Charles (Charles George Hildebrant)
and group of others try to survive against the creature and its offspring.

13
00:55:25,263 --> 00:55:31,263
The Deadly Spawn was shot in New Jersey on 16 mm film.

14
00:59:41,052 --> 00:59:47,052
The house in which the majority of the film takes place belonged to illustrator Tim
Hildebrandt, who also served as an executive producer on the film.

15
01:03:56,842 --> 01:04:02,842
John Dods served as associate producer and special effects director; the
effects work involved wire-controlled rubber puppets.

16
01:08:12,631 --> 01:08:18,631
Upon its release, in some territories, the film's title was changed to Return of the Aliens: The Deadly Spawn or The Return
of the Alien's Deadly Spawn in an attempt to capitalize on the worldwide success of the 1979 film Alien.

17
01:12:28,421 --> 01:12:34,421
The film explores themes of monster, camping, alien, alien invasion, parasite.

18
01:16:44,210 --> 01:16:50,210
The tone is dark and thought_provoking.
